// Excerpt from Tekla 2026.0 contentattributes_global.lst, trimmed for use as a test fixture.
// Real lines, verbatim: the definition lines for the attributes bound below, then a slice of the
// PART, BOLT and ASSEMBLY bindings — the ones a dump actually asks for (PROFILE, WEIGHT,
// PART_POS, ...) plus enough neighbours to exercise grouping and tier classification. The full
// file is 1.2 MB and 24k lines, which is more than a fixture needs to prove the parser reads the
// format.

